WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:11.345
OK, so,
here are a few things

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:13.972
you might have missed
while watching the movie.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.184
Let's go.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:22.147
One is the moment
that you see Cherokee Bill

00:00:22.231 --> 00:00:25.776
and Trudy Smith
walking past the train.

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:28.028
Take a moment

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:30.906
and read the name
of that train.

00:00:32.241 --> 00:00:35.452
C. A. Boseman.

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:37.287
Yes.

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:39.581
Chadwick Boseman.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:43.085
Rest in power, king.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.216
In the town,
in Redwood, you know,

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.301
if you look on the street

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:53.095
and you see the names
of the shops,

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:54.555
you know,
what James did is start

00:00:54.638 --> 00:00:56.807
to put family and friends,

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.143
and their names
became the shops.

00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:03.480
So, there's a Carter
and Carter general store.

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:05.274
You know
who the Carters are.

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:08.068
It's named
after Jay-Z and Beyoncé.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.363
And it's
an interesting thing.

00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:12.406
When I was naming those,

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:15.200
I was literally giving out
stores like a dictator,

00:01:15.284 --> 00:01:16.118
calling up people.

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:17.911
"What's your middle name?"

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.789
"We'll name that store
after you."

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:23.000
And I called Jay,
and I was like,

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.085
"Jay, what name
goes with Carter?"

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.462
He's like,
"What do you mean?"

00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:29.089
"What name
goes with Carter?"

00:01:29.173 --> 00:01:30.799
You know,
Jay's voice is kind of high,

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:31.800
it's aspirational.

00:01:31.884 --> 00:01:32.759
And he went,

00:01:33.886 --> 00:01:35.721
"Only one name
goes with Carter."

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.806
"What name's that?"

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.933
He went, "Carter."

00:01:41.602 --> 00:01:42.769
"Carter and Carter."

00:01:42.853 --> 00:01:43.770
I was like…

00:01:45.397 --> 00:01:47.399
"Carter and Carter
General Store."

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:49.610
There's a JL
Savings and Loan,

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:52.613
and James Lassiter
is the producer.

00:01:52.696 --> 00:01:53.906
He's a great producer
in Hollywood,

00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:54.948
people know him very well.

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:57.284
I wanted to have the bank,
but I didn't think about it,

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.827
you know,
when I had that idea.

00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:02.372
When we go to Douglastown,

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:04.625
and Nat Love is riding in,

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:07.419
you see a man
taking a picture

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.422
of another man in a coffin

00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:12.841
and you see
the name Rex Mills.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.219
And during COVID,

00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:17.304
I did an Instagram
murder mystery

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:21.099
that starred Jay-Z,
Ellen Pompeo,

00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:22.434
Tiffany Haddish,
Jesse Williams,

00:02:22.518 --> 00:02:23.352
Sterling K. Brown,

00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:25.687
Cynthia Erivo, Zazie Beetz,

00:02:25.771 --> 00:02:28.815
and it ended
with Morgan Freeman

00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:30.859
saying that he's Rex Mills.

00:02:30.943 --> 00:02:33.820
I am Rex Mills.

00:02:33.904 --> 00:02:36.740
And you see Rex Mills
in The Harder They Fall

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.159
and Morgan Freeman
plays Rex Mills.

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:41.912
There's just so many, like,
little things like that.

00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:47.543
Something else
you might have missed?

00:02:48.836 --> 00:02:49.878
I don't know
if you missed it,

00:02:49.962 --> 00:02:51.505
but it's just
a fun fact that…

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:54.174
I happen to walk around
with this thing

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.843
all the time.

00:02:57.094 --> 00:02:58.804
Here we are,
in the real world,

00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:01.348
and this is my cup.

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:02.933
This is also Nat Love's cup.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:06.395
And this is the cup
we drink out of in the film,

00:03:06.478 --> 00:03:07.437
throughout the film.

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:10.190
Never known you to touch it.

00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:13.819
Only after I kill a man.

00:03:16.572 --> 00:03:20.492
I mean, there's a huge
Easter egg in this film

00:03:20.576 --> 00:03:25.539
that I am not going
to tell you what the egg is.

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:26.874
It's huge.

00:03:29.084 --> 00:03:33.463
And it's where
I place music over film.

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:35.966
I'm not going to tell you
what it is,

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.342
but I'll tell you the song.

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:40.971
The song is "Blackskin Mile"

00:03:41.722 --> 00:03:43.515
by Cee-Lo,

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:48.478
But I know there's
Something better outside

00:03:48.562 --> 00:03:49.688
And it's…

00:03:50.314 --> 00:03:51.148
It's…

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.275
It plays at the end
and kind of…

00:03:56.278 --> 00:03:58.947
It kind of joins and moulds

00:04:00.115 --> 00:04:03.452
the storylines of Rufus Buck

00:04:03.535 --> 00:04:06.330
and Nat Love when he's bent
over Jim Beckwourth,

00:04:06.413 --> 00:04:10.667
and Cherokee Bill
when he faces Cuffee.

00:04:10.751 --> 00:04:12.169
And the song speaks of his…

00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:13.587
his…

00:04:14.838 --> 00:04:16.006
his state of mind.

00:04:16.882 --> 00:04:20.260
But there's a huge,
huge, huge Easter egg

00:04:20.344 --> 00:04:21.637
in that song.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.597
It's a code, and…

00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:26.975
I'll leave that to you guys
to find out.

